WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.000
[On screen] External & Internal Rotation

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
[On screen] Medial Rotation (Internal Rotation): a rotational movement towards the midline.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
[On screen] Lateral Rotation (External Rotation): a rotating away from the midline.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:39.000
[He turns his arms, then his legs, inward and outward.] Medial Rotation (Internal Rotation), Lateral Rotation (External Rotation)

00:00:39.000 --> 00:01:04.500
[He turns his bent leg and his raised arm inward and outward.] Medial Rotation (Internal Rotation), Lateral Rotation (External Rotation)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.000
[On screen] Dorsiflexion & Plantarflexion

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.000
[On screen] Plantarflexion: an extension at the ankle, so that the foot points inferiorly.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:25.500
[On screen] Dorsiflexion: flexion at the ankle, so that the foot points more superiorly.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:32.000
[On screen] Elevation & Depression

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
[He lifts his shoulders up.] Elevation: movement in a superior direction.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:46.500
[He lowers his shoulders down.] Depression: movement in an inferior direction.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.000
[On screen] Protraction & Retraction

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.000
[He pulls his shoulders back.] Retraction: the posteromedial movement of the scapula on the thoracic wall, which causes the shoulder region to move posteriorly.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:10.500
[He pushes his shoulders forward.] Protraction: the anterolateral movement of the scapula on the thoracic wall that allows the shoulder to move anteriorly.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:19.400
[On screen] Venue: Lion’s Park, Baguio City. Reference: teachmeanatomy.info, terms of movement.
